.TH INTRO 6
.SH NAME
intro \- introduction to file formats
.SH DESCRIPTION
This section describes file formats and conventions: the shape of a
program image on disk, the notation a document is typeset in, the
chords a keyboard and a mouse produce, and the files that carry a
convention rather than a service.
None of these is a device or a program.
Each is a way of reading bytes that something else writes and
something else reads back.
.PP
.IR Man (6)
is the macro package this manual is typeset in.
.IR Vx (6)
describes
.B VECTRA01
and
.BR VECTRA02 ,
the two shapes a program image takes on disk and in the kernel's own
pak.
.IR Keys (6)
lists the chords the draw server acts on.
.IR Workspaces (6)
describes the file that names a workspace's windows.
.IR Theme (6)
describes the toolkit's look as a file, read rather than compiled in.
.IR Keyboard (6)
describes what a key delivers at each layer between a scancode and a
line of text.
.IR Regexp (6)
is the regular expression notation
.B sys/libregex
matches.
.IR Kfs (6)
describes the on-disk shape of
.IR kfs (4),
Vectra's own file system.
